[ ] Protect the known critical semantics =protect-critical-semantics $Use focused valid-state generators and property tests, guided by mutation analysis, to protect the fixed inventory of reference-routing, template-targeting, and high-risk lifecycle invariants; retain precise examples only where exact bytes, diagnostics, interoperability, or escaped regressions are themselves contractual.$ !1 #019ffc5b-d063-76e0-be9d-93f1b50e2954
[ ] Retain only demonstrated test support =demonstrated-test-support $Keep local builders, properties, or conformance fixtures only where the concrete contract work demonstrates that they improve clarity or serve a second real consumer.$ !2 <protect-critical-semantics #019ffc5b-d06f-7d33-9d88-fa2890c59cf3
[ ] Validate the pinned platform composition =validate-pinned-platform $Provide one practical command that runs repository-owned checks against the exact submodule revisions pinned by the platform without introducing a generalized validation framework.$ !2 <protect-critical-semantics #019ffc5b-d07b-7653-b695-843c0e41a530
[ ] Record lessons and close executable assurance =close-executable-assurance $Record the useful commands and techniques, brief rationales for consequential residual risks, and evidence-based triggers for any future assurance charter, then review the done gate and close this charter.$ !3 <demonstrated-test-support <validate-pinned-platform #019ffc5b-d087-7d00-957d-46c4f82eb6cd
